{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftUITracking"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"SwiftUITracking","externalID":"SwiftUITracking","roleHeading":"Framework"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module to track events from SwiftUI views on Apple platforms; elsewhere it builds empty.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Set a tracker once, at the root of the views, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and read it in any view below","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Environment(\\.tracker)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A button’s action can track through it, which a ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binding can’t reach, since SwiftUI runs actions on tasks of its own. Until a tracker is set, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"environment holds ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.noOp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a preview tracks nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifiers track through the environment’s tracker, once per trigger, and record the place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they are applied as the call site. ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackOnAppear(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks each time a view appears,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each tap beside the view’s own action, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackChange(of:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each new value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each time the view appears, and puts a tracker enriched","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the screen’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the environment inside it, so every event tracked from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"screen carries its name:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftUI","","struct CartOpened: Event {}","","struct CheckoutStarted: Event {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        List {","            Button(\"Check out\") {","                tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))  \/\/ its record's context[ScreenKey.self] is \"Cart\"","            }","        }","        .trackOnAppear(CartOpened())","    }","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let root = CartView()","    .trackScreen(\"Cart\")  \/\/ tracks ScreenViewed(screen: \"Cart\") each time it appears","    .tracker(tracker)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apply "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreen(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" where the screen’s view is placed, as above, not in the view’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a view’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Environment"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the environment around it, which its own body’s modifiers don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Where UIKit has traits, the environment’s tracker is the same value as UIKit’s trait","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},{"text":"), so SwiftUI views hosted in UIKit read the scene’s tracker. For UIKit and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"AppKit views, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"To track screens without a modifier on each, see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers all three frameworks.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"API","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s API isn’t there, so its symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for an Apple target."}]},{"text":"Setting the tracker","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Setting-the-tracker"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EnvironmentValues.tracker","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.tracker(_:)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Tracking from views","type":"heading"